{"id": "EUVD-2026-15219", "enisaUuid": "8d08288a-8262-3097-9655-a5e8ec10bb6d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: usb: pegasus: validate USB endpoints\n\nThe pegasus driver should validate that the device it is probing has the\nproper number and types of USB endpoints it is expecting before it binds\nto it.  If a malicious device were to not have the same urbs the driver\nwill crash later on when it blindly accesses these endpoints.", "datePublished": "2026-03-25T10:26:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:13:42", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d5d9086211877361f1bda44a0aec538ddb04042a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af7369ae572f53cb701731a4289ec3b3889bc501", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43d7c4114b1ec14f41f09306525d3b9382286fc1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f8505c7ce3f186ef9d2495f3c0bd6ad6fce999f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/95556b4e879711693c9865ba0938c148f62d5ea4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3f1672eaea68c5cb6e1ec081cdb92045453218f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee31ec8cf1eafeefa85ef934ba688d27f88bf0e2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11de1d3ae5565ed22ef1f89d73d8f2d00322c699"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-23290", "GHSA-gpw9-p95r-3mv6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09f3d3f6-b009-3b23-9398-f549e823bf81", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <7f8505c7ce3f186ef9d2495f3c0bd6ad6fce999f"}, {"id": "0c67ed9d-1c1b-38eb-bf99-366e3030a2ca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <af7369ae572f53cb701731a4289ec3b3889bc501"}, {"id": "26a4d205-adfa-3efd-ab30-480fbe0b0660", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <ee31ec8cf1eafeefa85ef934ba688d27f88bf0e2"}, {"id": "2abdd68d-6592-3022-a0ad-ddf8c6b8